<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <PackageId>Enigma.Core</PackageId>
    <Version>2.0.0</Version>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Title>Enigma.Core — .NET Cryptography Library</Title>
    <Description>A modern, service- and factory-oriented .NET cryptography library built on BouncyCastle, designed for dependency injection. Provides block ciphers (AES, DES, 3DES, Blowfish, Twofish, Serpent, Camellia, CAST5, IDEA, SEED, ARIA, SM4) with ECB/CBC/CTR/GCM (incl. AAD) modes, stream ciphers (ChaCha20, ChaCha20-RFC7539, Salsa20), RSA (PKCS#1 v1.5 &amp; OAEP encryption, signing, PEM) over a reusable RsaKey handle, post-quantum cryptography (ML-DSA and ML-KEM, each with key PEM import/export and optional PBES2 encryption), X.509 certificates (generation, CSR, issuance, chain validation, CRL revocation, PKCS#12/DER import-export), hashing (MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-512, SHA-3), HMAC, CRC checksums (CRC-16 ARC/CCITT-FALSE/XMODEM/MODBUS/KERMIT and CRC-32 ISO-HDLC/CRC-32C, for error detection only), one-time passwords (HOTP/TOTP with otpauth provisioning), key derivation (PBKDF2, Argon2), padding schemes, and data encoding (Base64, Base32, Hex).</Description>
    <PackageTags>enigma cryptography bouncycastle aes chacha20 salsa20 rsa pqc ml-dsa ml-kem pem x509 certificate csr pfx sha hash hmac crc crc16 crc32 checksum otp hotp totp base32 pbkdf2 argon2 encryption signing dotnet</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.md</PackageLicenseFile>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/enigmalibs/Enigma.Core</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/enigmalibs/Enigma.Core</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>BREAKING: RSA key material now crosses the public surface as a reusable RsaKey handle instead of PEM text. Every PEM-string overload on IPublicKeyService was removed outright — nothing was deprecated, so there is no transition window — GenerateRsaKeyPair became GenerateRsaKey, and the per-call char[] password parameter is gone: a passphrase is supplied once, at RsaKey.ImportPrivateKeyPem. IX509CertificateService moved to the same handle, and ImportPkcs12 now returns (string certificatePem, RsaKey privateKey). Encrypted private keys are now written as PBES2 (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, AES-256-CBC); reading still accepts unencrypted PKCS#8, PBES2 and traditional-OpenSSL, so existing key files keep working — only the API breaks, not the files. New: ML-DSA and ML-KEM key PEM services, and a Checksum module with seven CRC-16/CRC-32 variants (error detection, never a security primitive). Still targets netstandard2.0/net8.0/net10.0 on BouncyCastle 2.7.0. See RELEASENOTES.md for the full details.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- Package README and LICENSE files, packed at the nupkg root. Paths are relative to this csproj
       at src/Enigma.Core/; PackageReadmeFile/PackageLicenseFile above reference them by file name. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!-- BouncyCastle backs every crypto implementation feature; referenced on all TFMs but never
       exposed on the public surface (see the reflection guard test). -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="BouncyCastle.Cryptography" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!-- System.Buffers (Span/Memory/ArrayPool support) is framework-provided on net8.0+; it is only
       needed as an explicit package on netstandard2.0. Referencing it on net8.0/net10.0 would raise
       NU1510 and fail the zero-warnings build. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="System.Buffers" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!-- PolySharp: polyfills modern C# on netstandard2.0. Compile-only (PrivateAssets=all). -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="PolySharp" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
